{
  "format": "waddle.behavior/v0",
  "name": "grant_demotion_hysteresis",
  "description": "Pins FSM.md §7 rules 1-4 (N6/N11): sustained bad gate-tick/callback-dispatch proxy signals crossing the declared hold latency bound must produce NO GrantStatusChange emission while the lease is active (rule 2 — no grant event of any kind in two 400 ms windows); after terminate{SUCCESS} ends the episode and the lease window, the deferred demotion of grants[VERB_HOLD] to GRANT_STATUS_DEMOTED is emitted with a populated effective_t_ns; signals then hovering just inside the bound must NOT re-promote (rule 3 hysteresis — no grant{to:ACTIVE} within 1 s); re-promotion lands only via a safe-window path, here a HeartbeatAck carrying the grant change to ACTIVE (rule 4: changes ride the ack as well as the stream). Judgment calls: rule 2 is pinned as deferral of the emission itself, not an early emission with future effective_t_ns; the demoted grant is VERB_HOLD (gate-tick and callback-dispatch jitter proxy the hold verb's health) and the bimanual fixture's declared hold bound is 40 ms with a 0.8 hysteresis ratio (good band below 32 ms) — the bad signals (p95 420 ms) are unambiguously over the bound, and the hovering signals (p95 36 ms) sit inside the (32 ms, 40 ms) hysteresis band: under the bound yet earning no recovery credit; effective_t_ns exceeding lease end is asserted temporally (the emission appears only after termination) plus $nonempty, since relational matchers do not exist.",
